  "_about": "WHITE RHINOCEROS (sculpt overlay, 2026-11-05): a grazer 1.8 m at the shoulder, 3.9 m head and body -- a nuchal hump before the withers, a deep barrel on short thick legs (fore folding at the wrist, hind at the hock), three-toed feet; the long head held low to a broad square lip, a long front horn curving back and a short rear one, tubular ears high on the skull; skin folds behind the shoulder, before the thigh and round the neck. (2026-11-08) The HORNS are the engine's sharp `horn` (sharp.js; tools/creaturegen/sharp/horns.py merged the field part and its slender detail tip into one centreline): smooth, sunk in the skull, a true point. (2026-11-08, fair_bases.py) The HORNS' roots are FAIRED into the skull (sharp.js horn `fair`): a small boss, the smooth union of horn and skin, no crease. (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): tall tubular cupped sheets (sharp.js `fin`), the edges rolled in, round-tipped; the roots faired.",
